## Summary

One frame for every admin page, and an admin home with real numbers: open complaints, AI recommendations waiting for a decision, riders suspended now, and the latest admin actions.

> Third of three. **Merge #42 (CS455-47) and #43 (CS455-48) first.** Until then this PR also shows those commits; the CS455-49 change is commit 7127e0b only.

### Changes

- **`AdminPageShell`:**
  - at the top, the admin navigation (Home, Complaints, Riders, Configuration, Profile) with the current page marked, and Log out;
  - then the page's title, with an optional back link, eyebrow, description and actions;
  - the pages in A5 and A7 use it.
- **Admin home** (`AdminHome`, `getAdminHome()`):
  - complaints awaiting review (submitted or under review, chat reports included), with the safety ones called out;
  - AI recommendations awaiting a decision (validated, undecided, on an open complaint; 0 until A9);
  - riders suspended now;
  - the last 10 audit entries: what, about whom or what, who, when, and Done, Refused or Failed;
  - SOS still says "Not available yet", and is no longer a link to a missing page.
- **For Mahir:**
  - `getAdminHome()` counted `ride_chat_complaints`; it now counts `complaints`. Your chat reports land there too (#42's trigger), so the count covers the same reports plus form complaints;
  - your `/admin/complaints` page is unchanged. A7 turns it into one queue for all complaints;
  - `admin-activity.ts` holds the action codes for `withAdminAction` and how the pages name them:
    - `vehicle_type.create` and `.update`, `location.create` and `.update`;
    - `campus_fare.set`, `external_fare.set`;
    - `complaint.status`;
    - `rider.warn`, `rider.suspend`, `rider.reactivate`;
    - `ai.decide`;
    - `role.grant` and `role.revoke` (operator script).

    Please use these in A4, A6 and A10, and add a code there when you need a new one.
- **`/admin`:** sends an admin to their home, and shows a student the "not for you" page (US-OA-19).
- **Routes:**
  - added `rideComplaint`, `myComplaints`, `adminComplaint`, `adminRiders`, `adminRider` and `adminRide` for A7;
  - "Incidents" leaves the admin navigation until SOS exists;
  - AI recommendations are decided on each complaint (A11), so they have no navigation entry of their own;
  - Riders and the complaint details come with A7, and Configuration with A5. Until then those links show the 404 page, as other links to unbuilt pages do.
- **README:** the routes table and the admin pages.

