## Summary

The configuration, complaint and enforcement APIs (A4 and A6 of CS455-46). PR #46 does not contain them: it adds a ride matcher, a test script and lockfile changes. So these are built here, to the contract we agreed in `admin-types.ts`, on top of `withAdminAction()` from #43. The configuration pages (#48) and complaint pages (#49) use them.

> First of three: merge this one first, then #48 (CS455-51), then #49 (CS455-53). Each targets master.

### Changes

- **Configuration (CS455-50)** (`src/lib/admin-config.ts`):
  - `POST /api/admin/vehicle-types` and `PATCH /api/admin/vehicle-types/[id]`;
  - `POST /api/admin/locations` and `PATCH /api/admin/locations/[id]`;
  - `PUT /api/admin/campus-fares`;
  - `PUT /api/admin/external-fares`.
  - **IDs:** a new item's ID comes from its name and never changes.
  - **Nothing is deleted:** an item is deactivated, leaves the ride forms, and stays on the rides that use it.
  - **Conflicts:** every edit sends the `version` it loaded, and a stale one gets 409 `version_conflict` with the item as it is now.
  - **Audit:** every change, refusal and failure is audited with before and after.
- **Complaints (CS455-52)** (`src/lib/complaints.ts`):
  - **`POST /api/rides/[id]/complaints`:**
    - only someone on the ride, about someone else on it, named by seat;
    - until 7 days after completion, or about a reported chat message at any time;
    - one per person, ride and accused; at most 5 in 24 hours;
    - answers 201 `{ reference }`.
  - **`PATCH /api/admin/complaints/[id]`:**
    - moves a complaint to Under review or Resolved; resolving needs `actionTaken`, and Resolved is final;
    - notifies the person who complained, saying only whether action was taken;
    - closes the chat reports the complaint came from.
- **Enforcement (CS455-52)** (`src/lib/enforcement.ts`):
  - `POST /api/admin/riders/[id]/warnings`, `.../suspensions` (a number of days, or `indefinite: true`) and `.../reactivation`;
  - each needs a reason, and the history is kept;
  - one suspension at a time, and admins cannot be warned or suspended;
  - the rider is notified with the end time and the reason category, never the admin's words.
- **Suspended riders** get 403 `suspended`, with the end time and reason category:
  - on `POST /api/rides`;
  - on the ratings API;
  - they can still file complaints (FR-RD-01.5).
- Parsers: `parseComplaintStatusChange()` and `canMoveComplaint()` in `complaint-rules.ts`, and the new `enforcement-rules.ts`.
- **Files of others (small additions):**
  - Khushi's `POST /api/rides` gains the suspension check, and her route test mocks it;
  - the chat report trigger from #42 still copies Mahir's chat reports into complaints, and his chat UI is unchanged.
- **Not in this PR:**
  - chat messages and search do not check suspensions yet (Mahir's socket code and #45's search);
  - the enforcement buttons are A8 (Mahir).

