## Summary

The complaint form and "Your complaints" for riders. For admins: one complaint queue, the complaint detail with its status actions, rider search, the rider record and a read-only ride.

> Third of three. **Merge #47 and #48 first.** Until then this PR also shows their commits; the CS455-53 change is commit 74e9924 only.

### Changes

- **Rider side:**
  - **`/rides/[id]/complaint`:**
    - who the complaint is about, by seat, the category, and what happened (20 to 2000 characters);
    - Safety shows 112 and the IIT Kanpur security number;
    - `?message=` reports a chat message (FR-RD-09.6);
    - outside the 7-day window it says why;
    - people already complained about are listed with their reference;
    - on success it shows the reference.
  - **Links to it:**
    - "Report a problem" on the ride page for 7 days after completion (`RideView.canComplain`);
    - the review page's low-score note, which used to give an email address.
  - **`/complaints`:**
    - the rider's own complaints, with status and, once resolved, whether action was taken (FR-RD-13.5);
    - linked from the student home.
- **Admin side:**
  - **`/admin/complaints`:**
    - one queue for form complaints and chat reports, Safety first, then the longest waiting;
    - filters for status, category and source, in a GET form, so a filtered view has its own URL.
  - **`/admin/complaints/[id]`:**
    - the complainant's words, exactly as filed;
    - the reported messages;
    - complainant and accused, linked to their records;
    - the ride;
    - the accused's other complaints (OA-FR-20);
    - Mark under review, and Resolve with whether action was taken and an optional note.
  - **`/admin/riders`:** search by name, email or roll number.
  - **`/admin/riders/[id]`:** identity, account status, rides, complaints filed and received, warnings and suspensions with who lifted them and why.
  - **`/admin/rides/[id]`:** read only.
- **TEAM, before D2:** `src/lib/emergency.ts` has the IIT Kanpur security number as `null`, and the page says "number to be confirmed". D1 does not give the number, so please fill it in.
- **For Mahir:**
  - your `/admin/complaints` page now renders the unified queue, as agreed when chat reports merged into complaints;
  - `ChatComplaintQueue.tsx` and `/api/admin/chat-reports` are no longer used by the page. I left both in place for you to keep or remove;
  - your page test is rewritten for the new page;
  - the enforcement buttons (A8) and the AI panel (A11) fit on the complaint detail and rider record pages.
- **Other people's files (small additions):** the review page note (`RatingForm`), "Your complaints" on `StudentHome`, and the "Report a problem" line on `RideDetails`.
- **Gotcha:** `src/index.css` styles every `<blockquote>` as a large landing-page quote, so these pages use plain paragraphs. It's noted in the README.

