41 cases that try to break the app through its real routes against a
real database; each must end in a clean refusal or a consistent state,
never a 500:

- time boundaries, a moment either side: the lock minute (request and
  search), the no-show grace period, the 7-day complaint window, the
  72-hour rating window, the end of the departure window;
- input: broken JSON, arrays, strings and null as bodies; wrong types
  not coerced; oversized keys, IDs and descriptions (up to 1 MB);
  malformed, injection-looking and unknown IDs answered 404 without a
  query; SQL and markup stored as plain text;
- replays: an idempotency key sent again with another ride or pickup
  point (found bug 2, fixed in the previous commit), double accept;
- actions out of order: on cancelled rides, after pickup started,
  after completion, after leaving;
- races, on separate connections: two accepts for the last seat, accept
  against withdraw, a five-fold double-click with one key, triple lock,
  five SOS taps, completion sent twice, the same offer twice;
- the per-address rate limit on offering a ride.

moveDeparture takes fractions of a minute, for the boundary cases.

